+// Records that a far transfer -- a far jump, far call or far return -- was
+// translated at this guest address. `Kind` must be a string literal; it is
+// stored by pointer and printed with the block that the transfer landed in.
+// Wine's WoW64 layer enters 32-bit code through an indirect far jump and
+// returns through another, and the translator lowers both as a RIP change plus
+// a stored cs_idx with no change of decode mode, so the block compiled after
+// one is the exact boundary where 32-bit code starts being decoded as 64-bit.
+// Bounded on its own budget: the block trace's budget is spent during startup,
+// long before the transfer worth watching.
+FEX_DEFAULT_VISIBILITY void BoxedWineNoteGuestFarTransfer(uint64_t GuestRIP, const char* Kind);
+// Returns and clears the address a pending far transfer was translated at, or
+// zero, writing its kind through `Kind` when one is pending. Counts the report
+// against the far-transfer budget.
